1
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
The 25th anniversary of the first public performance of Phantom of the Opera.

2
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
The Phantom of the Opera at the Royal Albert Hall is a music,
drama, romance film directed by Laurence Connor.

3
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
A disfigured musical genius, hidden away in the Paris Opera House, terrorises the opera
company for the unwitting benefit of a young protégée whom he trains and loves.

4
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
The 25th anniversary of the first public performance of Phantom of the Opera was
celebrated with a grand performance at the Royal Albert Hall in London.

5
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
The Phantom, played by Ramin Karimloo.

6
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Christine Daae, played by Sierra Boggess.

7
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Raoul, Vicomte de Chagny, played by Hadley Fraser.

8
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Madame Giry, played by Liz Robertson.

9
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Joseph Buquet, played by Nick Holder.

10
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Carlotta Giudicelli, played by Wendy Ferguson.

11
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The Phantom of the Opera at the Royal Albert Hall is a 2011 British concert film adaptation of the 1986 stage
musical The Phantom of the Opera by Andrew Lloyd Webber, itself based on the 1910 novel by Gaston Leroux.

12
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
To celebrate the 25th anniversary of the musical, three special performances on Saturday 1 October 2011 at 7.30pm and Sunday 2 October 2011
at 1.30pm and 7.00pm were filmed at the Royal Albert Hall, the third of which was screened live worldwide on 2 October 2011.

13
02:10:00,000 --> 02:10:06,000
For further releases, footage from all three performances was edited together.

14
02:20:00,000 --> 02:20:06,000
The film explores themes of opera, london, england,
paris, france, love triangle, musical.

15
02:30:00,000 --> 02:30:06,000
The tone is emotional.
